#. review_status: llm_draft
#. source_hash: e7326def
msgid "Tutorial 4: CostGrow and Model Comparison"
msgstr "Tutoriel 4 : CostGrow et comparaison de modèles"

#. review_status: llm_draft
#. source_hash: dac2a3f9
msgid ""
"This tutorial builds on Tutorial 2 by running the same sample data through both the built-in "
"``CostGrow_Terrain`` model and the downloaded ``ResUNet_16x_DEM`` model."
msgstr ""
"Ce tutoriel prolonge le tutoriel 2 en exécutant les mêmes données d'exemple avec le modèle "
"intégré ``CostGrow_Terrain`` et le modèle téléchargé ``ResUNet_16x_DEM``."

#. review_status: llm_draft
#. source_hash: 655e0012
msgid "By the end, you will have:"
msgstr "À la fin, vous aurez :"

#. review_status: human_locked
#. source_hash: b68f6bf2
#. reviewed_at: 2026-06-14
#. reviewer: Codex trivial-review
msgid "a CostGrow output raster"
msgstr "un raster de sortie CostGrow"

#. review_status: human_locked
#. source_hash: ad6eba23
#. reviewed_at: 2026-06-14
#. reviewer: Codex trivial-review
msgid "a ResUNet output raster"
msgstr "un raster de sortie ResUNet"

#. review_status: llm_draft
#. source_hash: 58138926
msgid "a comparison raster storing ``CostGrow - ResUNet``"
msgstr "un raster de comparaison contenant ``CostGrow - ResUNet``"

#. review_status: llm_draft
#. source_hash: 4ba76471
msgid "a side-by-side plot of the two model outputs"
msgstr "un graphique côte à côte des deux sorties de modèle"

#. review_status: human_locked
#. source_hash: 74e492d5
#. reviewed_at: 2026-06-14
#. reviewer: Codex trivial-review
msgid "Before you start"
msgstr "Avant de commencer"

#. review_status: llm_draft
#. source_hash: 33cd6e1e
msgid "This tutorial requires the extended install because ``CostGrow_Terrain`` depends on PCRaster."
msgstr "Ce tutoriel nécessite l'installation étendue, car ``CostGrow_Terrain`` dépend de PCRaster."

#. review_status: llm_draft
#. source_hash: 87e26f89
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**CLI (`pipx`)**: use the extended environment from {ref}`extended_install_cli`."
msgstr "**CLI (`pipx`)** : utilisez l'environnement étendu de {ref}`extended_install_cli`."

#. review_status: llm_draft
#. source_hash: 77c60a50
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**Local notebook (Jupyter)**: use the extended environment from {ref}`extended_install_notebook`."
msgstr "**carnet local (Jupyter)** : utilisez l'environnement étendu de {ref}`extended_install_notebook`."

#. review_status: llm_draft
#. source_hash: b3e822f0
msgid ""
"**Hosted notebook (Colab)**: not recommended for this tutorial because the extended stack is "
"heavier and less reliable."
msgstr ""
"**carnet hébergé (Colab)** : non recommandé pour ce tutoriel, car la pile étendue est plus lourde"
" et moins fiable."

#. review_status: human_locked
#. source_hash: 5e0740b6
#. reviewed_at: 2026-06-14
#. reviewer: Codex trivial-review
msgid "Install additional packages"
msgstr "Installer des paquets supplémentaires"

#. review_status: human_locked
#. source_hash: f494e4b4
#. reviewed_at: 2026-06-14
#. reviewer: Codex trivial-review
msgid "Prove the install"
msgstr "Vérifier l'installation"

#. review_status: llm_draft
#. source_hash: 5e5a0d0a
msgid "Let's check the versions now:"
msgstr "Vérifions maintenant les versions :"

#. review_status: human_locked
#. source_hash: 7df60b64
#. reviewed_at: 2026-06-14
#. reviewer: Codex trivial-review
msgid "Imports"
msgstr "Importations"

#. review_status: llm_draft
#. source_hash: 95b5fba7
msgid "Download the same test data as Tutorial 2"
msgstr "Télécharger les mêmes données de test que dans le tutoriel 2"

#. review_status: llm_draft
#. source_hash: 3b45a793
msgid ""
"We reuse the small sample rasters from the earlier tutorials so the comparison stays quick to run"
" and easy to inspect."
msgstr ""
"Nous réutilisons les petits rasters d'exemple des tutoriels précédents afin que la comparaison "
"reste rapide à exécuter et facile à examiner."

#. review_status: human_locked
#. source_hash: ab953a64
#. reviewed_at: 2026-06-14
#. reviewer: Codex trivial-review
msgid "Resolve the input paths"
msgstr "Résoudre les chemins d'entrée"

#. review_status: human_locked
#. source_hash: cb9ff6e8
#. reviewed_at: 2026-06-14
#. reviewer: Codex trivial-review
msgid "Fetch ResUNet weights"
msgstr "Récupérer les poids ResUNet"

#. review_status: llm_draft
#. source_hash: a12884d8
msgid ""
"``CostGrow_Terrain`` is built in, so it does not need a weights download. ``ResUNet_16x_DEM`` "
"does, so we fetch it once here before running the comparison."
msgstr ""
"``CostGrow_Terrain`` est intégré, il n'a donc pas besoin de téléchargement de poids. "
"``ResUNet_16x_DEM`` en a besoin, donc nous les récupérons une fois ici avant de lancer la "
"comparaison."

#. review_status: human_locked
#. source_hash: 153272e5
#. reviewed_at: 2026-06-14
#. reviewer: Codex trivial-review
msgid "Plot the tutorial inputs"
msgstr "Tracer les entrées du tutoriel"

#. review_status: human_locked
#. source_hash: c412a340
#. reviewed_at: 2026-06-14
#. reviewer: Codex trivial-review
msgid "Run CostGrow"
msgstr "Exécuter CostGrow"

#. review_status: llm_draft
#. source_hash: 1539854c
msgid ""
"Now run ``tohr`` with the built-in ``CostGrow_Terrain`` model. We set ``--window-method hard`` "
"explicitly so the tutorial reflects the current large-raster-safe CostGrow path."
msgstr ""
"Exécutez maintenant ``tohr`` avec le modèle intégré ``CostGrow_Terrain``. Nous définissons "
"explicitement ``--window-method hard`` afin que le tutoriel reflète le chemin CostGrow actuel "
"adapté aux grands rasters."

#. review_status: human_locked
#. source_hash: f5cb01e4
#. reviewed_at: 2026-06-14
#. reviewer: Codex trivial-review
msgid "Run the ResUNet baseline"
msgstr "Exécuter la référence ResUNet"

#. review_status: llm_draft
#. source_hash: 00aea0bb
msgid ""
"Next run the learned ``ResUNet_16x_DEM`` model on the same inputs so we can compare the two "
"outputs directly."
msgstr ""
"Exécutez ensuite le modèle appris ``ResUNet_16x_DEM`` sur les mêmes entrées afin de comparer "
"directement les deux sorties."

#. review_status: human_locked
#. source_hash: fd0d79ef
#. reviewed_at: 2026-06-14
#. reviewer: Codex trivial-review
msgid "Write a comparison raster"
msgstr "Écrire un raster de comparaison"

#. review_status: llm_draft
#. source_hash: 47a66141
msgid ""
"For a quick numeric comparison, we save a raster of ``CostGrow - ResUNet`` on the same grid as "
"the model outputs. Positive values indicate deeper predictions from CostGrow, and negative values"
" indicate deeper predictions from ResUNet."
msgstr ""
"Pour une comparaison numérique rapide, nous enregistrons un raster de ``CostGrow - ResUNet`` sur "
"la même grille que les sorties de modèle. Les valeurs positives indiquent des prédictions plus "
"profondes avec CostGrow, et les valeurs négatives indiquent des prédictions plus profondes avec "
"ResUNet."

#. review_status: human_locked
#. source_hash: 919a7f66
#. reviewed_at: 2026-06-14
#. reviewer: Codex trivial-review
msgid "Plot the results side by side"
msgstr "Tracer les résultats côte à côte"

#. review_status: llm_draft
#. source_hash: 8ad9744b
msgid ""
"The first three panels compare the input and the two high-resolution outputs. The fourth panel "
"shows the signed difference raster so you can quickly spot where the model outputs diverge."
msgstr ""
"Les trois premiers panneaux comparent l'entrée et les deux sorties haute résolution. Le quatrième"
" panneau montre le raster de différence signée afin que vous puissiez repérer rapidement les "
"zones où les sorties des modèles divergent."
